dashboard.definition:
{
  "title": "KO History",
  "description": "Version history for every knowledge object on this instance.",
  "dataSources": {
    "ds_kos": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "Knowledge objects tracked",
      "options": {
        "query": "index=`ko_history_index` | stats dc(title) as n",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "0",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_versions": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "Versions captured",
      "options": {
        "query": "| tstats count as n where index=`ko_history_index`",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "0",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_enabled": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "Capture searches enabled",
      "options": {
        "query": "| rest /servicesNS/-/ko_history/saved/searches splunk_server=local | search title=ko_* disabled=0 | stats count as n",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_started": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "Splunk last started",
      "options": {
        "query": "| rest /services/server/info splunk_server=local | eval started=strftime(startup_time,\"%F %T\"), uptime=tostring(now()-startup_time,\"duration\") | rename started as \"Splunk last started\", uptime as \"Up for\" | fields \"Splunk last started\" \"Up for\"",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_restore": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "Restore enabled for",
      "options": {
        "query": "| rest /servicesNS/nobody/ko_history/configs/conf-ko_history splunk_server=local | search title=restore | fields dashboard savedsearch macro eventtype fieldextraction lookup tag | transpose | search \"row 1\"=1 | stats count as n",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "-1m",
          "latest": "now"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_md_intro": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# KO History\n\nEvery dashboard, report, alert, macro, event type, field extraction, lookup\ndefinition and tag on this instance, snapshotted into `index=ko_history` on a\nschedule, so you can see what changed, who changed it, and put it back. The\nindex name is configurable on the **[Settings](ko_settings)** page.\n\n**[Open KO History](wrapper)** to browse version history, compare two versions\nside by side and restore one.\n"
      }
    },
    "viz_kpi_kos": {
      "type": "splunk.singlevalue",
      "title": "Knowledge objects tracked",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_kos"
      },
      "options": {
        "majorColor": "#00cdaf",
        "numberPrecision": 0
      }
    },
    "viz_kpi_versions": {
      "type": "splunk.singlevalue",
      "title": "Versions captured",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_versions"
      },
      "options": {
        "majorColor": "#00cdaf",
        "numberPrecision": 0
      }
    },
    "viz_kpi_enabled": {
      "type": "splunk.singlevalue",
      "title": "Capture searches enabled",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_enabled"
      },
      "options": {
        "majorColor": "#00cdaf",
        "numberPrecision": 0
      }
    },
    "viz_kpi_restore": {
      "type": "splunk.singlevalue",
      "title": "Restore enabled for",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_restore"
      },
      "options": {
        "majorColor": "#00cdaf",
        "numberPrecision": 0,
        "unit": "types"
      }
    },
    "viz_started": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Restart check",
      "description": "If you installed or upgraded KO History after this time, restart Splunk. Nothing prompts you to. Until you do, opening KO History or Settings returns a server error, usually a 500.",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_started"
      }
    },
    "viz_md_setup": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "## Is this install working?\n\nThe four numbers above answer that. What they should read on a healthy install:\n\n| Number | Healthy | If it is zero |\n|---|---|---|\n| Knowledge objects tracked | grows to match your instance | nothing has been captured yet |\n| Versions captured | grows over time | same, or the index is missing |\n| Capture searches enabled | 15 or more | the searches still ship disabled, see below |\n| Restore enabled for | 0 is a valid choice | restore is off, which is the default |\n\n**Setup is four steps**, in order:\n\n1. **Restart Splunk, if you have not since installing.** Nothing prompts you to,\n   on Splunk Cloud or on Enterprise, but the main page and the settings page do\n   not work until you do. See the note at the foot of this page for why.\n2. **Create the `ko_history` index.** On Splunk Cloud, create an Events index by\n   that name. On Enterprise the bundled `indexes.conf` does it for you. Already\n   have one under a different name, or need to? Set it below under **Index**,\n   which writes the `ko_history_index` macro every search reads.\n3. **Enable the capture searches.** They all ship disabled. The\n   **[Reports](reports)** tab lists them already scoped to this app. Enable the\n   seven `*_backup` searches and `ko_all_delete_audit`, then optionally the\n   seven `*_catchup` searches together with `ko_seen_kos_builder`.\n4. **Enable restore, if you want it.** It is off for every object type until an\n   admin turns it on, on the **[Settings](ko_settings)** page. Everything else\n   works without it.\n\nRun each `*_backfill` search **once**, by hand, to seed a snapshot of what\nalready exists. They are not scheduled, and re-running one duplicates snapshots.\n"
      }
    },
    "viz_md_where": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "## Where to go\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **[KO History](wrapper)** | The main page. Version history, side-by-side compare, restore. |\n| **[KO Version (Studio)](ko_version_ds)** | The data UI on its own: filters, KPIs, the object table, source and diff. |\n| **[KO Version (SXML)](ko_version)** | The Simple XML equivalent, with an in-place live render of a captured dashboard. |\n| **[Help and dependencies](ko_help)** | How the pieces fit together. Read before renaming a view or moving the index. |\n| **[Settings](ko_settings)** | Which object types may be restored, and which index the app reads. Admin only. |\n| **[Reports](reports)** | The capture searches, scoped to this app. |\n"
      }
    },
    "viz_md_restart": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "## Just installed, and something looks broken?\n\n**Restart Splunk.** Nothing will prompt you to. There is an app.conf setting\nthat makes Splunk raise the prompt itself, but AppInspect forbids it, so no\napp distributed through Splunkbase can use it. Confirmed on Splunk Cloud: the\ninstall completes with no prompt and no warning.\n\n**The symptom is a server error, usually a 500, when you open KO History or\nSettings.** Sometimes it is a stack trace mentioning\n`TopLevelLookupException` and a missing template. If either page errors, you\nhave not restarted since installing. Nothing else causes this.\n\nBoth are React pages served from a Mako template plus a static bundle, and\nSplunk resolves both when the appserver starts, so before a restart they cannot\nbe found. Reloading the app or refreshing the browser does not help. The same\napplies after an upgrade, where a stale bundle is worse than a missing one.\n\nThis page is deliberately plain Dashboard Studio so it works before that\nrestart, which is why it is the one the app opens on.\n"
      }
    }
  },
  "inputs": {},
  "layout": {
    "globalInputs": [],
    "tabs": {
      "items": [
        {
          "layoutId": "layout_1",
          "label": "Home"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "barPosition": "top",
        "showTabBar": false
      }
    },
    "layoutDefinitions": {
      "layout_1": {
        "type": "absolute",
        "options": {
          "width": 1280,
          "height": 1920
        },
        "structure": [
          {
            "item": "viz_md_intro",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 0,
              "w": 1280,
              "h": 210
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_kpi_kos",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 230,
              "w": 311,
              "h": 130
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_kpi_versions",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 323,
              "y": 230,
              "w": 311,
              "h": 130
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_kpi_enabled",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 646,
              "y": 230,
              "w": 311,
              "h": 130
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_kpi_restore",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 969,
              "y": 230,
              "w": 311,
              "h": 130
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_started",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 380,
              "w": 1280,
              "h": 150
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_md_setup",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 550,
              "w": 1280,
              "h": 620
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_md_where",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 1190,
              "w": 1280,
              "h": 330
            }
          },
          {
            "item": "viz_md_restart",
            "type": "block",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 1540,
              "w": 1280,
              "h": 360
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
